{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\_cls6_jpg\\geo\\035.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "2.9GridReference", "conf": 0.881, "box": [[100, 164], [414, 171], [413, 203], [99, 196]]}, {"text": "Grid references are points on a map that are used to find a location anywhere in the world.", "conf": 0.928, "box": [[97, 236], [1112, 253], [1111, 286], [96, 269]]}, {"text": "A network of vertical and horizontal lines drawn on maps to locate positions is called a grid.", "conf": 0.939, "box": [[93, 287], [1191, 303], [1190, 342], [92, 325]]}, {"text": "Vertical and horizontal lines.of a grid are labelled as Eastings and Northings respectively.", "conf": 0.932, "box": [[95, 325], [1087, 343], [1087, 375], [94, 358]]}, {"text": "Upward direction on a map established by Eastings of a grid is termed as Grid North.", "conf": 0.939, "box": [[97, 378], [1035, 394], [1034, 427], [96, 411]]}, {"text": "Eastings and northings are the standard names for the x and y coordinates in a planar coordinate", "conf": 0.928, "box": [[95, 431], [1191, 449], [1191, 481], [94, 463]]}, {"text": "system, while latitudes and longitudes are the standard names for the coordinates in a", "conf": 0.919, "box": [[96, 468], [1192, 486], [1192, 519], [95, 501]]}, {"text": "geographiccoordinatesystem.", "conf": 0.931, "box": [[96, 506], [446, 512], [446, 544], [95, 537]]}, {"text": "92", "conf": 0.62, "box": [[573, 629], [592, 629], [592, 645], [573, 645]]}, {"text": "93", "conf": 0.641, "box": [[794, 628], [821, 632], [818, 652], [792, 648]]}, {"text": "94", "conf": 0.553, "box": [[970, 631], [1000, 631], [1000, 657], [970, 657]]}, {"text": "qen", "conf": 0.513, "box": [[1071, 695], [1125, 695], [1125, 716], [1071, 716]]}, {"text": "86", "conf": 0.665, "box": [[89, 758], [116, 758], [116, 777], [89, 777]]}, {"text": "Garhi-", "conf": 0.741, "box": [[650, 757], [725, 757], [725, 777], [650, 777]]}, {"text": "86", "conf": 0.518, "box": [[1187, 811], [1213, 811], [1213, 832], [1187, 832]]}, {"text": "Besu", "conf": 0.714, "box": [